tests:
  unit: { count: 124, covers: "The shell's proxy reader returns Set, Off or Unreadable, and unreadable classifies as unknown with no address. macOS reads the first enabled proxy of any service, is off only when every service answered off, and cannot read without its service list or when a service failed with none enabled; a proxy beside a failed service still reads. Windows reads a switch that is off or never written as off, an enabled host:port as set, and reg failing to run, a missing server or one that is not one host:port (a per-scheme list) as unreadable. Linux and every other host have no reader. The scenario's unreadable proxy reads unknown and its unset one none. The platform table per host: macOS offers all eight, Windows, Linux and other offer seven with no iOS Simulator, the Android emulator is on every host; canProbe is macOS and Windows only. Quit takes the remote notice for unknown, the path none takes." }
  integration: { count: 212, covers: "P5 inverted (R8): the picker on Windows, Linux and an unknown host offers no iOS Simulator and does offer the Android emulator. R20: the probe row shows for this machine on macOS and Windows and not on Linux or an unknown host. R19: on Linux an unread proxy is the promise, never off. P7 inverted (R9): one address is named under address to use before arming. R21: the arm button and its warning name the chosen interface, and taking the other address renames the button. R22: no address gives the join-the-network remedy and a check again that calls the re-read, and dims tasks 2-4 without after step 1; in App, check again reads /reach anew and offers the arm button for the address it finds. R11: a guide closed on Another Mac does not stay closed on This machine, red before the tasks were keyed on the platform. The state matrix holds the place, time and truth rules over every offered host x platform state and sweeps no Simulator state off macOS." }
  e2e: { waived: "The owner waived the walkthrough for W5 (2026-09-27) and tests the build on the real hosts; W6 re-runs the walkthrough, whose R8, R9, R11 and R19-R22 chapters already caption this WU's expectations. The epic plan gives no e2e journey to W5." }
